The political message has to be simple: we already have universal health care. The problem is not having a rational way to pay for it. Look at how we pay for it: 

personal insurance premiums;
employer insurance premiums;
co-pays;
deductibles, and;
general taxes.

Impress on people the fact that they can’t make decisions based on one of those sources without accounting for its effect on other sources. Increased general taxes to pay for single-payer health care — which eliminates the need for employer and personal insurance premiums, is at worst revenue neutral for the average person.

The experience of France and Germany is that we would save 5 percent of GNP annually by moving to a single payer system. In the US, that’s $1.3 TRILLION a year.

Trump keeps lying about the state of the war.  Whether you like the war, or not, most don't, he has beena terrible wartime president.  Allowing Iran to dig in and re-arm was perhaps the most foolish thing he could have done.  This poem sums up the war.

For want of a nail, the shoe was lost;
For want of a shoe, the horse was lost;
For want of a horse, the rider was lost;
For want of a rider, the battle was lost;
For want of a battle, the kingdom was lost,
And all for the want of a horseshoe-nail.
